\n    `%USERPROFILE%\\.codex\\state_5.sqlite\n    %USERPROFILE%\\.codex\\state_5.sqlite-wal\n    %USERPROFILE%\\.codex\\state_5.sqlite-shm\n    %USERPROFILE%\\.codex\\session_index.jsonl\n    `\n\n  2. Update the SQLite row:\n    \n    update threads\n    set title = '<restored title>',\n        updated_at = <current unix seconds>,\n        updated_at_ms = <current unix milliseconds>,\n        archived = 0,\n        archived_at = null\n    where id = '<thread_id>';\n\n  3. Update or add the corresponding `session_index.jsonl` record:\n    \n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nResume and fork fail after `$HOME` changes because SQLite retains a stale rollout path · Issue #47002 · openai/codex (https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/47002)\nciteturn4search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 days ago; Crawled: today; Confirm that the session transcript now exists at `/home/alice/.codex/sessions/.../rollout-<thread-id>.jsonl` while the corresponding threads.rollout_path value in state_5.sqlite still points to `/home/owner/.codex/sessions/.../rollout-<thread-id>.jsonl` ... Codex should recognize that the explicitly discovered rollout under the current CODEX_HOME belongs to the requested thread, rebind or repair the stale database path, and successfully resume or fork the session. ... github-actions\n\n  6. Confirm that the session transcript now exists at `/home/alice/.codex/sessions/.../rollout-<thread-id>.jsonl` while the corresponding threads.rollout_path value in state_5.sqlite still points to `/home/owner/.codex/sessions/.../rollout-<thread-id>.jsonl`\n\n  7. Run: `codex resume <thread-id>`\n\n  8. Run: `codex fork <thread-id>`\n\n### What is the expected behavior?\n\nCodex should recognize that the explicitly discovered rollout under the current CODEX_HOME belongs to the requested thread, rebind or repair the stale database path, and successfully resume or fork the session.\n\n### Additional information\n\nResume fails even