*) FROM threads WHERE archived=0 AND archived_at IS NOT NULL;\"\n\nExpected (current actual behavior): archived count is back near pre-UPDATE baseline; the `archived=0 AND archived_at NOT NULL` \"smoking gun\" count is 0 (the timestamp is cleared along with the flag).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCodex Desktop and CLI sharing CODEX_HOME causes local provider state and CLI threads to leak into Desktop · Issue #39195 · openai/codex · GitHub (https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/39195)\nciteturn4search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: today;     thread_history_1.sqlite ...     state_5.sqlite ...     `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Packages\\OpenAI.Codex_2p2nqsd0c76g0\\ ... Therefore, I cannot conclude that a specific SQLite, JSONL, rollout, or LevelDB file alone was responsible for the stale Recent entries.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCodex Desktop Windows: archive fails with os error 2 when state_5.sqlite rollout_path uses \\\\?\\ prefix · Issue #39669 · openai/codex · GitHub (https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/39669)\nciteturn4search7 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: yesterday; # Codex Desktop Windows: archive fails with os error 2 when state_5.sqlite rollout_path uses \\\\? ... https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/main/codex-rs/thread-store/src/local/archive_thread.rs\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\ncodex/codex-rs/rollout/src/state_db.rs at main · openai/codex · GitHub (https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/main/codex-rs/rollout/src/state_db.rs)\nciteturn4search8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; // rollouts for one thread and cannot know which one SQLite selected. ... let restore_memory_mode_from_rollout = ... context: Option<&codex_state::StateRuntime>,\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCodex local history index becomes stale and re